{"id":"7e4596c4-5d6c-489c-a531-168b4dc89344","object":"chat.completion","created":1784826667,"model":"deepseek-v4-flash","choices":[{"index":0,"message":{"role":"assistant","content":"{\"implementation\": \"def solve(case):\\n    import json\\n    # Validate and extract payload\\n    payload = case.get('payload')\\n    if not isinstance(payload, dict):\\n        raise ValueError('Missing payload')\\n    nodes = payload.get('nodes')\\n    required_symbols = set(payload.get('required_symbols', []))\\n    if not isinstance(nodes, list) or not nodes:\\n        raise ValueError('Invalid or empty nodes')\\n    # Build node dict and children mapping, validate fields\\n    node_dict = {}\\n    children = {}\\n    for node in nodes:\\n        if not isinstance(node, dict):\\n            raise ValueError('Node is not a dict')\\n        nid = node.get('id')\\n        parent = node.get('parent')\\n        symbol = node.get('symbol')\\n        depth = node.get('depth')\\n        removable = node.get('removable')\\n        utility = node.get('utility')\\n        if any(x is None for x in (nid, parent, symbol, depth, removable, utility)):\\n            raise ValueError('Node missing required field')\\n        if not isinstance(nid, str) or not isinstance(parent, (str, type(None))):\\n            raise ValueError('Invalid id or parent type')\\n        if not isinstance(symbol, str):\\n            raise ValueError('Invalid symbol type')\\n        if not isinstance(depth, int) or depth < 0:\\n            raise ValueError('Invalid depth')\\n        if not isinstance(removable, bool):\\n            raise ValueError('Invalid removable type')\\n        if not isinstance(utility, (int, float)):\\n            raise ValueError('Invalid utility type')\\n        node_dict[nid] = {'id': nid, 'parent': parent, 'symbol': symbol,\\n                          'depth': depth, 'removable': removable, 'utility': utility}\\n        if nid in children:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Duplicate node id {nid}')\\n        children[nid] = []\\n    # Build parent->children links\\n    for nid, nd in node_dict.items():\\n        p = nd['parent']\\n        if p is None:\\n            continue\\n        if p not in node_dict:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Parent {p} not found for node {nid}')\\n        children[p].append(nid)\\n    # Ensure exactly one root (parent None)\\n    roots = [nd for nd in node_dict.values() if nd['parent'] is None]\\n    if len(roots) != 1:\\n        raise ValueError('Must have exactly one root')\\n    root_node = roots[0]\\n    if root_node['symbol'] not in required_symbols:\\n        raise ValueError('Root symbol must be in required_symbols')\\n    # Verify all required symbols present initially\\n    initial_symbols = {nd['symbol'] for nd in node_dict.values()}\\n    for sym in required_symbols:\\n        if sym not in initial_symbols:\\n            raise ValueError(f'Required symbol {sym} not present in any node')\\n    # Initial retained set (all node IDs)\\n    retained = set(node_dict.keys())\\n    # Sort nodes by depth descending, then by node ID (string) ascending\\n    sorted_nodes = sorted(node_dict.values(), key=lambda nd: (-nd['depth'], nd['id']))\\n    removal_order = []\\n    for nd in sorted_nodes:\\n        nid = nd['id']\\n        if nid not in retained:\\n            continue\\n        # Cannot remove root\\n        if nd['parent'] is None:\\n            continue\\n        # Cannot remove nodes that are not removable\\n        if not nd['removable']:\\n            continue\\n        # Cannot remove nodes with required symbol\\n        if nd['symbol'] in required_symbols:\\n            continue\\n        # Cannot remove nodes that still have retained children\\n        if any(child in retained for child in children.get(nid, [])):\\n            continue\\n        # All conditions satisfied; remove the node\\n        retained.remove(nid)\\n        removal_order.append(nid)\\n    # Produce output\\n    retained_sorted = sorted(retained)\\n    return {'retained': retained_sorted, 'removal_order': removal_order}\\n\"}","reasoning_content":"We need to produce a Python function `solve(case)` that implements a grammar-guided node reduction algorithm. The task is to reduce a parse tree (given as nodes with parent, depth, symbol, removable, utility) while preserving required symbols, following a specific order: deeper nodes first, then tie-break by node ID. The algorithm: tentative removal of a node if its removal does not cause loss of required symbols and if the node is not root, not required symbol, and not having retained children? Actually the description: \"Never remove the root, a required symbol, or a node with retained children.\" Means we cannot remove a node that has children that are retained (i.e., not removed). So we need to simulate removal step by step: we have a set of retained nodes initially all nodes. For each candidate node (in order: deeper depth first, then stable tie break by node ID), we consider tentatively removing it. Removal is allowed if: node is not root, not required symbol? Actually root is always required as per required_symbols includes \"root\"? Usually root is required. Also nodes with symbol that is in required_symbols cannot be removed. Also nodes that have retained children? The problem says \"never remove ... a node with retained children.\" So if a node currently has any retained children, it cannot be removed. But also we need to ensure that after removal, all required symbols are still represented in the retained set. So we check: before removing, we check if required_symbols are still present after removal (excluding the node's own symbol, but also its descendants if they are removed? Actually if we remove a node, we also remove all its descendants? The tree reduction typically removes a node and its whole subtree? The problem description: \"Reduce a registered parse tree through grammar-valid deletion and replacement candidates while preserving an i